# The memory recall eval's hand set (plan 373dec00, step 1). Forty real
# knowledge records — ten each of bug, decision, how and spec — sampled
# across the whole date range of .coding/knowledge/ (2026-08 to 2027-01).
# Each line is one JSON object:
#   {"q": "<question>", "expect": ["<knowledge file stem>", ...], "kind": "<kind>"}
#
# The questions are written the way a user would ask them WITHOUT having seen
# the record: paraphrased, never reusing the title's distinctive words. The
# lead reads every question on review; a fixture that copied titles would
# flatter the score. `expect` may name several stems when sibling records
# answer the question equally. Superseded records are not used — default
# recall excludes them, so a question about one could never be answered.
